{"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "1. Produce fluorescent ICAM-1-displaying VLPs (along with control VLPs using empty vector and the ICAM-1 E34A mutant) by seeding 5 x 10^6 HEK293T cells per 10 cm dish in complete DMEM (DMEM + 10% heat-inactivated FBS + 10 mM HEPES). Incubate overnight to reach 70\u201380% confluence. Co-transfect cells with 8 \u00b5g of psPAX2 fluorescent plasmid (mNeon, eYFP, TagBFP, or mScarlet) and 4 \u00b5g of expression plasmid (wild-type pCMV6-ICAM-1, E34A mutant, or empty vector) using 36 \u00b5L X-tremeGENE 9 in 1 mL total Opti-MEM. Replace media with 10 mL fresh complete DMEM after 16\u201324 hours, and incubate for another 24 hours.\n\n2. Harvest culture supernatant at 48 hours post-transfection and pass through a 0.45 \u00b5m syringe filter. Mix 9 mL of filtered supernatant with 3 mL of Lenti-X Concentrator and incubate overnight at 4 \u00b0C. Centrifuge at 1,500 \u00d7 g for 45 minutes at 4 \u00b0C, thoroughly aspirate the supernatant, and resuspend the pellet in 90 \u00b5L PBS to yield a 100\u00d7 VLP stock. Aliquot and store at -80 \u00b0C or use immediately.\n\n3. For the binding assay, harvest target cells (THP-1, parental Jurkat, \u03b1L KO Jurkat, or our submitted cell samples) and resuspend directly in serum-free binding buffer (RPMI + 0.1% BSA) at 1\u20132 \u00d7 10^6 cells/mL. Dispense 50 \u00b5L of cell suspension per well into a 96-well V-bottom plate (50,000\u2013100,000 cells/well).\n\n4. Add 50 \u00b5L of 2\u00d7 Mg2+/EGTA activation solution (10 mM MgCl2, 4 mM EGTA in binding buffer) to each well. Immediately add 1\u20135 \u00b5L of concentrated VLP stock per well (titrate as needed for optimal signal-to-background ratio) and mix. Incubate at 37 \u00b0C for 10 minutes.\n\n5. Fix cells by adding 33 \u00b5L of cold 4% PFA to each well (1% final PFA concentration) and incubate on ice for 20 minutes. Centrifuge the plate at 350 \u00d7 g for 3 minutes, remove supernatant, and wash twice with 250 \u00b5L FACS buffer (PBS + 0.2% BSA).\n\n6. Resuspend the cell pellets in 200 \u00b5L FACS buffer per well and analyze VLP binding signal using flow cytometry.", "thoughtSignature": ""}], "role": "model"}, "finishReason": "STOP", "index": 0}], "usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 5781, "candidatesTokenCount": 648, "totalTokenCount": 8245, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 5781}], "thoughtsTokenCount": 1816, "serviceTier": "standard"}, "modelVersion": "gemini-3.6-flash", "responseId": "zKr2arfLNaz4-sAPyrOC8AY"}